class:: Tonnetz
summary:: Six-dimensional tonal centroid
categories:: UGens>Analysis>Tonal
related:: Guides/MIRa, Classes/HPCP, Classes/HarmonicPeaks, Classes/Pitch2

description::
Implements the tonal-centroid projection of Harte, Sandler and Gasser (2006), DOI 10.1145/1178723.1178727. The L1-normalized chroma weights three sine/cosine circles: angular steps 7*pi/6, 3*pi/2 and 2*pi/3, with radii 1, 1 and 0.5. MIRa returns the sine component before cosine in each pair. C-first chroma is required; using an A-first vector rotates the geometry. Silence maps to the origin.



classmethods::
method:: kr
argument:: chroma
A C-first Array of 12, 24, 36, or 120 nonnegative pitch-class values. Higher resolutions fold to nearest semitones where a twelve-class representation is required.

argument:: trig
A positive value processes this control block. For FFT-derived features pass chain >= 0 so each analysis frame is used once; default 1 processes each control block.

returns::
An Array: fifth sine/cosine, minor-third sine/cosine, major-third sine/cosine coordinates.

examples::
Tonnetz implements the 6D tonal-centroid projection of Harte, Sandler & Gasser (2006), projecting pitch classes onto 3 harmonic circles (Fifths, Minor Thirds, Major Thirds). In this example, the 6D coordinates steer spatial panning and filter resonant cutoffs of a secondary ambient texture. An interactive code::MIRaGUI.tonnetz:: displays the 2D planar projection of harmonic motion.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIRaGUI.soundPath("piano-chords.wav");
    ~miraBuffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~miraBus = Bus.control(s, 6);
    s.sync;
    ~miraExample = {
        var source = if(~miraBuffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~miraBuffer, BufRateScale.kr(~miraBuffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic chords fallback
            Mix.ar(SinOsc.ar([261.63, 329.63, 392.00, 523.25] * LFNoise0.kr(0.5).range(1, 1.25))) * 0.15
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(2048), source, 0.25);
        var chroma = HPCP.kr(chain, size: 12, harmonics: 2, normalize: \max, fftSize: 2048);
        var position = Tonnetz.kr(chroma, chain >= 0);
        var pan = position[0].lag(0.08);
        var tone = SinOsc.ar(220 * (position[2].lag(0.08) * 7).midiratio, 0, 0.05);
        var sound = Pan2.ar(tone, pan) + (source * 0.25 ! 2);

        if(~miraBus.notNil) { Out.kr(~miraBus, position) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2)
    }.play;

    ~miraGUI = MIRaGUI.tonnetz("Tonnetz Trajectory", ~miraBus);
});
)
::
code::
(
~miraExample.free;
if(~miraGUI.notNil) { ~miraGUI.close };
if(~miraBus.notNil) { ~miraBus.free };
if(~miraBuffer.notNil) { ~miraBuffer.free };
)
::
